    "review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::exporter_order_dict_duplicated": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::exporter_order_dict_duplicated",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Exporter sort-order dict defined identically in two sibling modules; updating one silently diverges from the other",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "convention_outlier",
        "related_files": [
          "app/eventyay/agenda/views/schedule.py",
          "app/eventyay/agenda/views/utils.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "schedule.py ScheduleView.exporters() (lines 251-266) defines `order = {'google-calendar': 0, 'webcal': 1, 'schedule.ics': 10, ...}` with 13 entries and then calls `.sort(key=sort_key)`.",
          "utils.py build_public_schedule_exporters() (lines 155-161) defines an almost identical `order = {'google-calendar': 0, 'webcal': 1, ...}` dict with the same 13 entries and calls `all_exporters.sort(key=lambda e: (order.get(e.identifier, 50), ...))`.",
          "The two sort implementations also differ in how they handle unlisted exporters: schedule.py distinguishes 'my-' prefix exporters (bucket 150) while utils.py assigns them all bucket 50 \u2014 a behavioral inconsistency masked by the apparent duplication."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract a single `EXPORTER_SORT_ORDER` module-level constant (or a `get_exporter_sort_key()` function) in utils.py that both ScheduleView.exporters() and build_public_schedule_exporters() import. Decide whether the 'my-' prefix bucket-150 split in schedule.py is intentional and, if so, apply it to utils.py too.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "e75059f0"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Fixed: extracted _dispatch_state_action() to collapse 5 identical @action methods; removed debug comment; extracted EXPORTER_SORT_ORDER constant; fixed meta_info_data to return {} on TypeError; extracted _extract_bearer_token() to deduplicate JWT header parsing.",
