      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "get_tickets_for_order uses bare 'except:' to silently skip ticket generation failures, returning a partial list with no caller signal",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "app/eventyay/base/services/tickets.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 180, 216: bare 'except: logger.exception(\"Failed to generate ticket.\")' inside a loop \u2014 the function continues and returns whatever tickets succeeded",
          "Callers (e.g. mail_send_task) proceed to attach the partial ticket list without knowing some tickets were missing \u2014 the recipient may receive an email missing expected attachments"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace bare 'except:' with 'except Exception:'. Consider returning a list of (filename, content, error) tuples or raising a PartialTicketError so callers can decide whether to proceed or abort. At minimum, log the order/position identifier alongside the exception so operators can correlate failures.",
