    "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::checkin_show_post_permission_mismatch": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::checkin_show_post_permission_mismatch",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "CheckInListShow declares read permission at class level but POST handler performs write operations requiring can_change_orders",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "authorization_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "app/eventyay/control/views/checkin.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "CheckInListShow sets `permission = 'can_view_orders'` (line 29) \u2014 the EventPermissionRequiredMixin enforces this at dispatch time for all HTTP methods including POST.",
          "CheckInListShow.post() (lines 125-220) creates and deletes Checkin objects (write operations), and checks `if 'can_change_orders' not in request.eventpermset` as a runtime guard (line 126). A user with only `can_view_orders` passes the mixin gate and enters the POST body.",
          "Sibling write views in the same file (CheckinListCreate, CheckinListUpdate, CheckinListDelete) correctly declare `permission = 'can_change_event_settings'` at the class level, which is the consistent pattern across the rest of the codebase."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either (a) set `permission = 'can_change_orders'` on CheckInListShow and handle the GET with a separate view or by checking can_view_orders inline for GET, or (b) use the same split-permission pattern as the API (define separate get/post dispatch based on required permission) so that POST requests are rejected at the mixin gate rather than inside the handler body.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "04dd60c6"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Added clarifying comment to CheckInListShow: GET requires can_view_orders; POST additionally requires can_change_orders (checked in post()). The pattern is intentional and now documented.",
