    "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::middleware_supported_partial_init": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::middleware_supported_partial_init",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "_supported module global in base/middleware.py is None until get_language_from_request() runs, but get_language_from_user_settings() reads it unconditionally",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "app/eventyay/base/middleware.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Line 26: '_supported = None' at module scope.",
          "get_language_from_request() (line 144-145) sets _supported on first call: 'if _supported is None: _supported = OrderedDict(settings.LANGUAGES)'.",
          "get_language_from_user_settings() (line 93-95) accesses '_supported' directly: 'if lang_code in _supported' \u2014 if called before get_language_from_request() has run, _supported is None and 'in None' raises TypeError.",
          "In practice, LocaleMiddleware.process_request() always calls get_language_from_request() first, which calls get_language_from_user_settings() internally, so the hazard is latent. But any direct call to get_language_from_user_settings() from a test or a new code path will fail."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move the _supported initialization into a standalone private function and call it from both get_language_from_request() and get_language_from_user_settings(). Alternatively, initialize _supported eagerly as 'OrderedDict(settings.LANGUAGES)' at module scope (safe because settings are finalized before middleware modules are imported under Django's normal startup).",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "ca0386fa"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
