      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "TALK_HOSTNAME computed from settings at module import time in event.py, creating stale-snapshot risk",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "app/eventyay/base/models/event.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Line 84: TALK_HOSTNAME = settings.TALK_HOSTNAME \u2014 this is evaluated once when the module is first imported",
          "Any test using override_settings(TALK_HOSTNAME=...) or any code that reads settings after the module is cached will see the original value, not the overridden one"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Remove the module-level constant. Access settings.TALK_HOSTNAME directly at call sites, or define a small accessor function: def get_talk_hostname(): return settings.TALK_HOSTNAME. This costs negligible runtime overhead and is consistent with Django best practice of not caching settings at module level.",
